{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge","id":1009497,"title":"The Traditions in Charge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-28T14:59:20-08:00","id":1009497,"title":"The Traditions in Charge","content":"I had an idea for a Mage setting I was hoping to get some help on.<br /> <br /> In the wake of 9/11 (totally sleeper based) a powerful Technocratic Cabal was destroyed and the Technocracy lost a primary power base. A few of the most numerous Traditions (the Order of Hermes, Virtual Adepts, Chorus, and Akashic Brotherhood) in New York City was able to get an alliance to oust the Technocracy in the city.<br /> <br /> The Traditions have been able to hold parts of New York City since but their hold is tenuous at best. As the alliance starts to crack because of ideological differences, the Technocracy is starting to make headway against them.<br /> <br /> The game starts as the Traditions begin to lose ground and the Tradition leadership becoming more draconian.<br /> <br /> Is this possible? Any ideas of how to make this work? How the Traditions could hold the city for so long? How the area would be affected by Tradition magic in charge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2788-armos-black","name":"Armos Black","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T18:05:01-08:00","id":1009579,"title":"","content":"You are going to need to throw a &quot;wall&quot; around NYC in some way to keep the Technocratic Union from POURING in and dealing with something like that. Particularly when pretty much anything they would need to do they would be able to explain away pretty easily in the wake of 9/11 under any number of different rationales. (And yeah, that means using Correspondence and Dimensional Science to get in.) <br /> <br /> Kinda like when there was the earthquake and Gotham City was abandoned to the various Batman villains to divvy up. There has to be a reason why the government didn't come in and restore order. (Or the cheap ass version that was using the Dark Knight movie...)<br /> <br /> But, hey, it actually makes the game easier to set up. You've got a classic sandbox environment with hard boundaries. Despite the fact that Brucato maintains that &quot;Mage is not a city-based game&quot; it can easiy work as one, particularly if leaving the city is a HUGE deal. Like &quot;Escape from New York&quot; level deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:25:41-08:00","id":1009705,"title":"","content":"The Union 'POURING' in is putting it mildly. New York is one of THE power bases of the Technocracy in modern times.<br /> It has Wall Street. It has the United Nations headquarters. It has a Federal Reserve Bank. Over 60 normal banks have their headquarters in NYC.<br /> J.P. Morgan, Goldman Sachs, Pfitzer Pharmaceuticals, Time Warner, Universal, Verizon, Viacom, HBO, Bloomberg, Citigroup, NBC, and and..<br /> <br /> The Technocracy wouldn't just try to pour into NYC, it would reinstate the Pogrom globally and dial it to 11. Heck, it could be a case for a Code Ragnarok Lite.<br /> <br /> ...that Traditions group should really, REALLY think thrice before attempting something as blatant as this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-29-2016, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:53:01-08:00","id":1009712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1009579#post1009579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are going to need to throw a &quot;wall&quot; around NYC in some way to keep the Technocratic Union from POURING in and dealing with something like that. Particularly when pretty much anything they would need to do they would be able to explain away pretty easily in the wake of 9/11 under any number of different rationales. (And yeah, that means using Correspondence and Dimensional Science to get in.)<br /> <br /> Kinda like when there was the earthquake and Gotham City was abandoned to the various Batman villains to divvy up. There has to be a reason why the government didn't come in and restore order. (Or the cheap ass version that was using the Dark Knight movie...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Some kind of ward against hypertech that disables HIT-Marks, cybernetics, plasma guns, Dimensional Science and much of Correspondence: Data? It can only be kept up for as long as the Traditions cooperate, as each of them is doing their part in the effect(s). They also receive lots of Quintessence from the outside to maintain it - the Technocracy must first track and disable the Quintessence supply. Until then, the Technocracy has to rely on NWO infiltration skills, Progenitor drugs, and Enforcer wits.<br /> <br /> You can always say that the Technepandi are sabotaging the Technocracy's efforts - or, to put it in another way, the Traditions got Nephandic support..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:25:44-08:00","id":1009720,"title":"","content":"One way to do it would be to locally change the Consensus to primal reality, so that any Technocrats that come by are vulgar and the Traditions aren't. With sufficient manpower and confusion about the changing Consensus in the high levels of the Technocracy, the Traditions could hold the city for at least a while. That might be more than you want for your game, though...do you really want people dying in the streets because the hospitals can't do modern medicine any more, and the dozen Verbena in the city have to run makeshift classes on how to make poultices?<br /> <br /> Another way is to create some sort of patron. Maybe the ludicrously powerful vampire prince of NYC suddenly hates the Technocracy for some reason and sends coteries to root them out. The Traditions might get some breathing room while the Technocracy breaks out the orbital mirrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:50:25-08:00","id":1009723,"title":"","content":"A possibility is for Traditions to entrench themselves within gangs: <a href=\"http://interactive.nydailynews.com/2015/12/gangs-of-new-york-city-interactive-map/\" target=\"_blank\">http://interactive.nydailynews.com/2...teractive-map/</a> . Traditionalists could even reveal bits of the truth to the gang members - like exposing a Technocrat to a gang; showing the changing IDs, the advanced bugs, the credit card which can withdraw as much as you want... Men in Black aren't so tough when you have men on the streets looking to take it to the Man! Gang members could also count as Sleeper witnesses to help disable hypertech. And they could be charmed and directed with Mind and/or Entropy.<br /> <br /> Having New York City Father (City Fathers are in Werewolf, but I assume that Mage also has them as it makes lots of sense.) on their side could help. The whole thing might have started because Traditions are looking to become more Umbra-capable in cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-29-2016, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:51:52-08:00","id":1009724,"title":"","content":"You may try to make some sort of ward that actually use the Technocracy streght against themselves...<br /> For example,<br /> lets say that, in that chaos a group of Traditions' &lt;sappers&gt; creep in and &quot;un-sanitize&quot; the main Node used by the Technocracy, then link a &quot;backdoor&quot; ward to this Node. The Technocracy is interested in mantaining strong and active this Node, to the point of giving up other Nodes to mantain this one.<br /> On the other side, when an outside Technocrat group try to teleport inside, this &quot;ward&quot; reject and maybe even damage them, thus consuming power from the Node.<br /> The inside Technocrats notice a loss of power and panick, pouring more power in the Node (to them appears that something from outside &quot;attacked&quot; the Node) and as the various parts of Technocracy rarely communicate with each other, they will need a LOT of time to figure out the trick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:33:02-08:00","id":1009778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1009720#post1009720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to do it would be to locally change the Consensus to primal reality, so that any Technocrats that come by are vulgar and the Traditions aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>In..<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> ..in New York City. Primal consensus. How on earth would you even come close to doing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:27:48-08:00","id":1009850,"title":"","content":"I am thinking this might be a little unrealistic in the setting of Mage.<br /> <br /> But I love the idea of the City Father aiding the Traditions. Might be the City Father is trapped or compelled as I see the City Father as a Technocratic aid. Also a deal with powerful Nephandi that the rest of the Traditions do not know about. One of the Tradition Mages supports the Nephandi through illicit means, sacrifices or something. (should we help the Technocracy against the corrupt Tradition Mages?) The node idea may work attached to a Nephandi Realm? Is it the Book of Chantrys that has information on a Technocratic prison connected to NYC?<br /> <br /> Maybe if I just make the Tradition area Manhattan to have the area they need to protect smaller?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2788-armos-black","name":"Armos Black","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T14:22:09-08:00","id":1009937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Armos Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1009850#post1009850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking this might be a little unrealistic in the setting of Mage.<br /> <br /> But I love the idea of the City Father aiding the Traditions. Might be the City Father is trapped or compelled as I see the City Father as a Technocratic aid.</div> </div> </div> </div>City Fathers very much don't have to be aligned to Technocracy's idea of a city. (Though I see how it feels appropriate, and in my view several City Parents might indeed favor Technocracy.)<br /> While the 'average' Verbena, Chorister, Euthanatos, Dreamspeaker or Akashic might not feel at ease in a city's center, this does not make Traditions as a whole anti-urban. Imagine a cabal of an Etherite, a Virtual Adept, a Hermetic, and two Cultists of Ecstasy - certainly appropriate emissaries to the urban Umbra. You can add urban shaman Dreamspeaker, as well. (Or more Ecstatics.)<br /> <br /> Add to this that Technocracy only since the last few decades is starting to delve into Spirit more openly (Though I can see them having a secret Spirit-related division since Order of Reason times.) Technocracy could have easily made a blunder like trying to give a tradition and culture-minded City Father chiminage in the form of money from the Syndicate. Or insulting Cockroach - thinking it's a weak spirit. This would be even worse blunder if you do a crossover with Werewolf...but even without Glass Walkers, Cockroach could still be more powerful than Technocracy judged.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps Technocracy played their cards right (the Syndicate together with some Iteration-Xers could certainly impress an urban Spirit Sovereign), but the Tradition representatives were still deemed a better prospect for an alliance by the City Father; it's hard to compete with Ecstatics and Virtual Adepts advised on umbral etiquette by a Hermetic. Following this, the Technocrats in New York received orders to sever the experimental ties with the denizens of Umbra, and to prepare to act against both the Traditionalists and the City Father.<br /> However, the Amalgam(s) involved in trying to court the City Father went AWOL, refusing to act against him or the Tradition members. They didn't join the Traditions, but they are using their newfound expertise in Spirit - and some impressive Technomagick bordering on mysticism - to ward New York, including it's Umbra. Those rebelling Technocrats want the higher-ups (And other Technocrats, including those at the Front Lines.) to reconsider their stance on treating Traditions and spirits - at the very least, the urban ones.<br /> The Traditions take advantage of both this split in the Technocracy, and their newfound alliance with New York City Father, to claim the city as theirs. A standoff ensues. Technocratic leadership currently hasn't yet decided how to act against the rebelling Technocrats - they lack full and proper information about their status and capabilities.<br /> Is this realistic enough ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:01:04-08:00","id":1009953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1009778#post1009778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In..<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> ..in New York City. Primal consensus. How on earth would you even come close to doing that?</div> </div> </div> </div>GM fiat, since there's no reality war mechanics in the books to represent changing the Consensus locally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:12:25-08:00","id":1009959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1009720#post1009720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to do it would be to locally change the Consensus to primal reality, so that any Technocrats that come by are vulgar and the Traditions aren't. With sufficient manpower and confusion about the changing Consensus in the high levels of the Technocracy, the Traditions could hold the city for at least a while. That might be more than you want for your game, though...do you really want people dying in the streets because the hospitals can't do modern medicine any more, and the dozen Verbena in the city have to run makeshift classes on how to make poultices?<br /> <br /> Another way is to create some sort of patron. Maybe the ludicrously powerful vampire prince of NYC suddenly hates the Technocracy for some reason and sends coteries to root them out. The Traditions might get some breathing room while the Technocracy breaks out the orbital mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's not really NYC anymore is it? That's a post-apocalyptic game. New York may be the setting, but there would be nothing really recognizable other than buildings that didn't fall down. <br /> <br /> Mages vs. vamps is a contest until the mages know what's going on. Then it's lots of &quot;Eat sunlight&quot; and &quot;Whoops, did you just get teleported out of your haven at noon onto the top of the Chrysler Building? So, sorry....&quot; and, if the kid glovers aren't off... well... dragonsbreath rounds that blow through walls, all of the vampires in the city suddenly having their property repossessed or subject to eminent domain and all the permits go through so amazingly fast that what starts at the start of business ends at demolition by noon... Oh, and mages that aren't stupid pretty much always know what's going on. Level 1 Spheres are INSANELY good at detecting things. Time 2 even before it happens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T23:30:49-08:00","id":1010070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1009953#post1009953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GM fiat, since there's no reality war mechanics in the books to represent changing the Consensus locally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, actually M20 dedicates a whole chapter to the nature of reality zones and changing local consensus <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Usually it involves time and investment into trying to change the hearts and minds of the local populance in regards to what they do and do not accept as possible - primal magick or technology.<br /> <br /> Hence my scepticism regarding New York. The city *is* probably divided into a lot of smaller reality zone groupings along the lines of Irrationality Zones, haunted spots, the nature of certain areas and spots at night, but..changing NYC into a primal reality zone? That'd take an insanely, INSANELY powerful act of willworking and mind Magick.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> That said - I *have* pondered one way to actually put a HUGE dent into reality in favor of willworking and miracles in NYC.<br /> Armos mentioned that the whole scenario is more or less in the wake of 9/11. The whole world's eyes was on NYC and Ground Zero.<br /> <br /> What if suddenly the towers had been rebuilt, live on TV, in a Miracle?<br /> <br /> That alone could make for an intense Mage campaign and what-if setting. Consider the stakes: Unlike the Week of Nightmares, this location was square and center of every live news broadcast in the west for weeks. A chance for the Traditions to get straight, realtime access to countless people through the Technocracy's own ways of information and propaganda. And even a few seconds of broadcast are enough, shuld the Technocray pull all the plugs - if they can in time.<br /> <br /> Now, the risk is insanely high: Rebuilding everything in front of everybody, in the course of a few moments, would take an insane amount of successes, and even more preparation to ward of insane amounts of Paradox Backlash along the lines of the Czar Vargo incident.<br /> Even more so, most of the preparations couldn't be done on-site because of sleeper and Technocratic security everywhere, so it'd need a plan for preparing big-time in advance, then infiltrating an area dripping with tension and vigilance, and suddenly performing the last part of that great ritual. Extraction is another can of worms entirely, but this act alone could have been a major, major turning point in the Ascension War. Insane risk, potential but not guaranteed insane reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T05:03:27-08:00","id":1010153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1010070#post1010070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A chance for the Traditions to get straight, realtime access to countless people through the Technocracy's own ways of information and propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple TV broadcasts are now deemed as being of the Technocracy ?:&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1010070#post1010070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said - I *have* pondered one way to actually put a HUGE dent into reality in favor of willworking and miracles in NYC.<br /> Armos mentioned that the whole scenario is more or less in the wake of 9/11. The whole world's eyes was on NYC and Ground Zero.<br /> <br /> What if suddenly the towers had been rebuilt, live on TV, in a Miracle?<br /> <br /> That alone could make for an intense Mage campaign and what-if setting. Consider the stakes: Unlike the Week of Nightmares, this location was square and center of every live news broadcast in the west for weeks. A chance for the Traditions to get straight, realtime access to countless people through the Technocracy's own ways of information and propaganda. And even a few seconds of broadcast are enough, shuld the Technocray pull all the plugs - if they can in time.<br /> <br /> Now, the risk is insanely high: Rebuilding everything in front of everybody, in the course of a few moments, would take an insane amount of successes, and even more preparation to ward of insane amounts of Paradox Backlash along the lines of the Czar Vargo incident.<br /> Even more so, most of the preparations couldn't be done on-site because of sleeper and Technocratic security everywhere, so it'd need a plan for preparing big-time in advance, then infiltrating an area dripping with tension and vigilance, and suddenly performing the last part of that great ritual. Extraction is another can of worms entirely, but this act alone could have been a major, major turning point in the Ascension War. Insane risk, potential but not guaranteed insane reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has the feeling of Mage hubris. 9/11 is such a tragedy because so many people died in a malicious attack. Rebuilding the towers does not help the dead and the injured in the slightest. (Unless you count giving Wraiths Fetters, but Sleepers won't know about this.) In the worst case, it would be seen as mocking the victims, their families and friends, and the USA. Did anyone ask the Mages to rebuild it? I dunno if the sudden awareness that Magick is possible would be enough to counterbalance the potential distaste; especially once the Technocracy mobilizes to counteract.<br /> I can especially see religious and faithful people as considering the rebuilding to be the work of Satan. Humans lives are taken, but the building standing for finance and consumerism is given back to the humanity! Technocracy can use this sentiment to target any Mages who out themselves.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be better to try the Super Bowl or the Olympics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-30-2016, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T11:55:19-08:00","id":1010286,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of positives for the Traditions in seizing all of NYC from the Technocracy. In one blow they crack the Syndicate's global infrastructure and the NWO's media network. They open one of the biggest travel locations as a melting pot of ideas and cultures. The subsequent crash devastates many parts of the world, giving the Trads an opportunity to step in and show alternate ways of living. It's a bold move that has two major drawbacks:<br /> <br /> 1) The reprisals from the Technocracy would be massive.<br /> 2) They would have to ruin the lives of a lot of sleepers to do it.<br /> <br /> The first is bad, the second is worse. Some Trad members would be okay with that kind of collateral damage, many would not.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there is an occupation of NYC that is even more effective for the Traditions. The Technocracy gets to keep their infrastructure, but the Traditions hold the rest of the city. This leaves much of the Technocracy infrastructure intact, but that infrastructure can be monitored and sometimes even used by the Traditions. By not isolating the city, they give their new reality machinations a chance to spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:14:53-08:00","id":1011128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1010286#post1010286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of positives for the Traditions in seizing all of NYC from the Technocracy. In one blow they crack the Syndicate's global infrastructure and the NWO's media network. They open one of the biggest travel locations as a melting pot of ideas and cultures. The subsequent crash devastates many parts of the world, giving the Trads an opportunity to step in and show alternate ways of living. It's a bold move that has two major drawbacks:<br /> <br /> 1) The reprisals from the Technocracy would be massive.<br /> 2) They would have to ruin the lives of a lot of sleepers to do it.<br /> <br /> The first is bad, the second is worse. Some Trad members would be okay with that kind of collateral damage, many would not.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there is an occupation of NYC that is even more effective for the Traditions. The Technocracy gets to keep their infrastructure, but the Traditions hold the rest of the city. This leaves much of the Technocracy infrastructure intact, but that infrastructure can be monitored and sometimes even used by the Traditions. By not isolating the city, they give their new reality machinations a chance to spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can the Traditions use the Technocracy infrastructure without changing it so much that it's effectively gutting it and, effectively causing all the problems that you postulate? <br /> <br /> The biggest example: Wall Street is set up entirely along Syndicate lines. Sure, it's possible to exploit that system, but those exploits (VA data manipulation, House Fortunae statistical manipulation, anoyone using Time 2 or Entropy 2, etc.) don't really change the Syndicate's system, they USE it. Wall Street and all those little tricks and games Wall Street people play with economics are all the Syndicate dug so deep into their Foci and Instruments that you can't even see the tips of their toes. Other mages (particularly Tradition types) don't use those Foci and Instruments, and, even when they do, they don't do so from the &quot;same place&quot;. (Yeah, there is definitely something above/beyond mages' personal foci... Someting associated with their Sect that is sort of a mini-Consensus zeitgeist that creates the &quot;Hermetic-ness&quot; of the OoH, and so on....) There are essential aspects of Wall Street that function because the Syndicate is pushing, prodding, tweaking, massaging, manipulating, breaking, fixing, etc. their big &quot;machine&quot;. Can House Fortunae take up the slack for that? And what would that look like? Would the &quot;new brokers' start seeming like fortune (ha!ha!) tellers using complex diagrams, magical numerological formula, gematria, etc. while structuring their bids in Arabic, Sanskrit, Ancient Greek, Egyptian, Persian and Enochian? Even if that is going on behind closed doors, won't the mundanes of Wall Street have to realize that something BIG has happened and things don't work the way they used to? Or even the way they are working in Hong Kong, Chicago, etc.? That lack of confidence in the system is enough right there to bring it crashing down. The panic as most of the big firms go down when NOTHING works right anymore... The new players and the attempts to co-opt them into the current power structure.... <br /> <br /> I have to admit, I really do love my image of the &quot;New Wall Street&quot; as recast by House Fortunae.... But if I try to think about it without a really artificial sense of isolation that ignores the interconnectedness of things, that Wall Street is going to come crashing down and, due to it's fundamental incompatibility with the rest of the world economy as dictated by the Syndicate that didn't get ousted, isn't going to climb out of that hole. Perhaps the Syndicate can do significant damage control and, say, shift the focus of the world economy elswhere, but, in that case, there is definitely a second part to the game.... The mess OUTSIDE this New New York....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T11:11:44-08:00","id":1011146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011128#post1011128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can the Traditions use the Technocracy infrastructure without changing it so much that it's effectively gutting it and, effectively causing all the problems that you postulate?<br /> <br /> The biggest example: Wall Street is set up entirely along Syndicate lines. Sure, it's possible to exploit that system, but those exploits (VA data manipulation, House Fortunae statistical manipulation, anoyone using Time 2 or Entropy 2, etc.) don't really change the Syndicate's system, they USE it. Wall Street and all those little tricks and games Wall Street people play with economics are all the Syndicate dug so deep into their Foci and Instruments that you can't even see the tips of their toes. Other mages (particularly Tradition types) don't use those Foci and Instruments, and, even when they do, they don't do so from the &quot;same place&quot;. (Yeah, there is definitely something above/beyond mages' personal foci... Someting associated with their Sect that is sort of a mini-Consensus zeitgeist that creates the &quot;Hermetic-ness&quot; of the OoH, and so on....) There are essential aspects of Wall Street that function because the Syndicate is pushing, prodding, tweaking, massaging, manipulating, breaking, fixing, etc. their big &quot;machine&quot;. Can House Fortunae take up the slack for that? And what would that look like? Would the &quot;new brokers' start seeming like fortune (ha!ha!) tellers using complex diagrams, magical numerological formula, gematria, etc. while structuring their bids in Arabic, Sanskrit, Ancient Greek, Egyptian, Persian and Enochian? Even if that is going on behind closed doors, won't the mundanes of Wall Street have to realize that something BIG has happened and things don't work the way they used to? Or even the way they are working in Hong Kong, Chicago, etc.? That lack of confidence in the system is enough right there to bring it crashing down. The panic as most of the big firms go down when NOTHING works right anymore... The new players and the attempts to co-opt them into the current power structure....<br /> <br /> I have to admit, I really do love my image of the &quot;New Wall Street&quot; as recast by House Fortunae.... But if I try to think about it without a really artificial sense of isolation that ignores the interconnectedness of things, that Wall Street is going to come crashing down and, due to it's fundamental incompatibility with the rest of the world economy as dictated by the Syndicate that didn't get ousted, isn't going to climb out of that hole. Perhaps the Syndicate can do significant damage control and, say, shift the focus of the world economy elswhere, but, in that case, there is definitely a second part to the game.... The mess OUTSIDE this New New York....</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines of the Technocracy still holds Wall Street and the News Media, and to the extent that the Traditions use those elements, they use them as is. The exploitation would be more along the lines of tapping into the systems and using them or analyzing them in ways the Technocrats aren't prepared for. Which is pretty much the state of things now, except that controlling the rest of the city gives the Traditions a few more opportunities.<br /> <br /> It would be an interesting world where the Traditions managed to subvert or replace one of the Technocracy's main pieces of infrastructure, but I doubt that would happen unless the Traditions controlled a significant percent of the major western cities. In the scenario I am suggesting they've just managed to quarantine the Technocracy into it's strongholds. Their success relies on the Technocracy as a whole underestimating just how successful they've been and that means leaving the Stock Market (and other things) alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:25:26-08:00","id":1011190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011146#post1011146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking more along the lines of the Technocracy still holds Wall Street and the News Media, and to the extent that the Traditions use those elements, they use them as is. The exploitation would be more along the lines of tapping into the systems and using them or analyzing them in ways the Technocrats aren't prepared for. Which is pretty much the state of things now, except that controlling the rest of the city gives the Traditions a few more opportunities.<br /> <br /> It would be an interesting world where the Traditions managed to subvert or replace one of the Technocracy's main pieces of infrastructure, but I doubt that would happen unless the Traditions controlled a significant percent of the major western cities. In the scenario I am suggesting they've just managed to quarantine the Technocracy into it's strongholds. Their success relies on the Technocracy as a whole underestimating just how successful they've been and that means leaving the Stock Market (and other things) alone.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So the whole thing smacks of just replacing vampires with mages and using the set up from the Original World of Darkness...<br /> <br /> The problem with that is... well, there are lots of problems. Like why two buildings blowing up is going to subvert the authority, much less the actual magical power of the Union and, conversely, why that same scenario should give Traditions mages opportunities to take any sort of power held by the Technocracy in mortal society, much less how such an event could promote the many different paradigms of the Traditions over that of Technocracy. And if it's more a matter of BOOM! BOOM! go the planes, BOOM! BOOM! the towers fall, and, for some reason, that weakens the Union's paradigm, so that, effectively, the Traditions all get a &quot;boost&quot; by default..... Well, that means all the mortal stuff that goes along with the Union's paradigm is going to take a hit, probably an initial one, particularly dealing with technological connections with the outside world and, probably, over time, a general degeneration of the underlying pervasive technological infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Assuming the situation as originally laid out, this seems less like a &quot;Cool! Tradition mages don't have to worry about the Man, anymore! Let's chat about it on our cellphones, go get some lattes and post pics on Instagram of some little ritual magics we do out in open, BECAUSE WE CAN! &lt;Insert rude hand gestures at absent Technocrats&quot;, and more &quot;OMG! OMG! The towers are fall....&quot; (static... then dead air as all cell phones and other forms of radio communication go dark... forever) set-up for a Post-Apocalyptic game with hard scramble Tradition mages trying to carve out enclaves, the most successful of which are going to be based around the paradigms of singular Traditions, with all sorts of enclave to enclave politics and conflict and lots and lots and LOTS of people suffering and dying and trying to escape...<br /> <br /> And, if those things aren't true, there is really no way to keep the Technocrats from coming back in... They've got Correspondence, too. Plus all the other ways creative mages can do that sort of thing, particularly when they've fundamentally rigged reality to ease their way.<br /> <br /> To get the particular feel I am reading into the OP, you are going to have to be very careful. There has to be a reason the Union can't just show back up. There has to be a way to keep the city intact so that it feels like an &quot;NYC&quot; game (Friends meets Mage?) and not a game set in something that is somewhat like NYC but, for most purposes, is something completely &quot;other&quot; with NYC landmarks. Those two are hard to balance against each other within the constraints of Mage's fluff and crunch....<br /> <br /> Maybe the blast released &quot;something&quot; that is creating a &quot;get the F out Union&quot; field. (Was it intentional? Was 9/11 really a Taftani act of reality insurgency? Or is it something to do with history of NYC? There are a LOT of weird things in the history NYC that might play well into something like that.... Or even something to do with why the Lenape might have been willing to sell Manhattan in the first place.... Hells, could be both. Stuff gets complicated fast.) Maybe the Union is still able to send in Extraordinary Citizens to keep its interests going. Maybe some of the new Traditions leadership in town realize that it's going to take letting the Union hold onto things like Wall Street and the UN, etc. even if they have to do so by proxy, or else the city/world is going to go to Hell in a handbasket. A new group promoting a parallel to the Union status quo, backed by the Law of Shadow... Meet the new boss(es), same as the old boss.... Sets up a nice conflict with these status quo high and mighty and some Trad mages who see opportunities to make &quot;real&quot; change (and damn the consequences... or, &quot;let's examine my careful ten point plan to make NYC a Hermetic wet dream without making it into something like the shell of a city in the midst of a war&quot;). Fun for the PCs to get caught up in. Plus, you KNOW the Union is trying to take this down from the outside... carefully. Or else they might be breaking what they are buying,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T04:02:36-08:00","id":1011447,"title":"","content":"The only way this would work would be if there was a destabilizing influence in the Technocracy that was on the scale of a technocratic civil war or something.<br /> <br /> The Avatar Storm and the battle with Ravnos Antediluvian would provide the necessary blow to the Technocracy... but only temporarily, unless they were continually kept down afterwards.<br /> <br /> As Ambrosia said, the Technocracy would start POURING in to NYC pretty fucking fast and it would be willing to allow some very dangerous procedures to rescue the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:46:37-08:00","id":1011645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011447#post1011447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way this would work would be if there was a destabilizing influence in the Technocracy that was on the scale of a technocratic civil war or something.<br /> <br /> The Avatar Storm and the battle with Ravnos Antediluvian would provide the necessary blow to the Technocracy... but only temporarily, unless they were continually kept down afterwards.<br /> <br /> As Ambrosia said, the Technocracy would start POURING in to NYC pretty fucking fast and it would be willing to allow some very dangerous procedures to rescue the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily.... <br /> <br /> Just one idea: 9/11 was a massive sacrifice to an Incarana level Umbrood and the result was some kind of magical barrier to members of the Union that encircles the city. The details can be filled in as needed. (Like who was performing the sacrifice and why. Did they get the result they wanted or was the Umbrood playing djinn and gave them something that fulfilled the letter of the bargain but not the intent? Etc.)<br /> <br /> Sure, the Union might be putting effort into getting back in, but there is a law of diminishing returns. They want to reclaim NYC and, if doing so meant, say, deploying something akin to solar mirrors or spirit nukes, they would balk. A fast solution is likely to be one that won't accomplish the goal. So... watch and wait and study and plot. For now. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:56:58-08:00","id":1011682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011645#post1011645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one idea: 9/11 was a massive sacrifice to an Incarana level Umbrood and the result was some kind of magical barrier to members of the Union that encircles the city. The details can be filled in as needed. (Like who was performing the sacrifice and why. Did they get the result they wanted or was the Umbrood playing djinn and gave them something that fulfilled the letter of the bargain but not the intent? Etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could go with an infernal ritual provided by a Demon Lady or a Lord. The anguish of the injured, terror of the dieing, despair of the families and people in general... generated the power, while the WTC's symbolic (and perhaps literal, if a Construct was in or near it) connection to the Technocracy provided the direction to the ban keeping Technocracy out for x years. (in various ways - from dementia-causing nightmares, through space manipulation, to outright misfortune happening to Technocrats in NYC)<br /> <br /> I'd make it a work of a Tradition &quot;the ends justify the means&quot; demonologist(s). It remains to be discovered whether the demonologist(s) organized the 9/11 attack themselves, or merely used what would already happen as a focus for the ritual. In the former case they are guilty of wrongdoing as well - as they could have prevented it, instead of preparing a ritual to reap the terror and anguish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:19:44-08:00","id":1011722,"title":"","content":"Considering the source, it could just as easily be a Taftani that decided to insert their own spin on the terrorists' plan and have the Umbrood involved be a powerful djinn. Or, even, Iblis, for the fallen angel angle. With the deal being more along the lines of &quot;end the foul magics of the West&quot; with an appropriately djinn twist on the execution of the bargain... Or maybe a bargain the Persian deity/Zoorastrian force Atar and the whole field is his/its interpretation of &quot;purifying&quot; the city... Or... I dunno. I'm sure I can think of a few more. <br /> <br /> And not have to involve Infernalism or Nephandi or whatever, as that adds a fundamental taint to the whole setting that needs to be thought through. Adding that in means, that ultimately, the whole setting is founded upon &quot;evil&quot; which means, as far as plot goes, it's going to have to be reversed or those who know and do nothing are complicit and tainted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T01:48:03-08:00","id":1011907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011722#post1011722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the source, it could just as easily be a Taftani that decided to insert their own spin on the terrorists' plan and have the Umbrood involved be a powerful djinn. Or, even, Iblis, for the fallen angel angle. With the deal being more along the lines of &quot;end the foul magics of the West&quot; with an appropriately djinn twist on the execution of the bargain...</div> </div> </div> </div>The catch could be &quot;Technocracy can't get in, but any mystic Mages inside can't get out.&quot;..dunno how it would end up this way, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T08:54:04-08:00","id":1012027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011907#post1011907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The catch could be &quot;Technocracy can't get in, but any mystic Mages inside can't get out.&quot;..dunno how it would end up this way, though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because Incarnae can just do that sort of thing using ST fiat. Hence having the Union take it apart is going to be difficult. Particularly if it's supposed to be anti-Technocracy-style magic in nature. (So, ya know, the Union can't just aport in personal or effects to deal with the issues.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T01:14:32-08:00","id":1012444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011645#post1011645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily.... <br /> <br /> Just one idea: 9/11 was a massive sacrifice to an Incarana level Umbrood and the result was some kind of magical barrier to members of the Union that encircles the city. The details can be filled in as needed. (Like who was performing the sacrifice and why. Did they get the result they wanted or was the Umbrood playing djinn and gave them something that fulfilled the letter of the bargain but not the intent? Etc.)<br /> <br /> Sure, the Union might be putting effort into getting back in, but there is a law of diminishing returns. They want to reclaim NYC and, if doing so meant, say, deploying something akin to solar mirrors or spirit nukes, they would balk. A fast solution is likely to be one that won't accomplish the goal. So... watch and wait and study and plot. For now. </div> </div> </div> </div>When I said you couldn't run the plot without a destabilizing influence on the union I was including examples like your own.<br /> <br /> After all, such an incidence would destabilize the union... In New York.<br /> <br /> I actually really like the idea of a major incarna getting in the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T04:56:16-08:00","id":1012496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1011190#post1011190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the whole thing smacks of just replacing vampires with mages and using the set up from the Original World of Darkness...<br /> <br /> The problem with that is... well, there are lots of problems. Like why two buildings blowing up is going to subvert the authority, much less the actual magical power of the Union and, conversely, why that same scenario should give Traditions mages opportunities to take any sort of power held by the Technocracy in mortal society, much less how such an event could promote the many different paradigms of the Traditions over that of Technocracy. And if it's more a matter of BOOM! BOOM! go the planes, BOOM! BOOM! the towers fall, and, for some reason, that weakens the Union's paradigm, so that, effectively, the Traditions all get a &quot;boost&quot; by default..... Well, that means all the mortal stuff that goes along with the Union's paradigm is going to take a hit, probably an initial one, particularly dealing with technological connections with the outside world and, probably, over time, a general degeneration of the underlying pervasive technological infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going to admit, I was dropping a lot of the 9/11 side of the story. There aren't many scenarios where that event leads to the Traditions having control of NYC. Even fewer where they have that level without kicking the Technocracy out or getting major metaphysical backing. Increased government presence, vigilance for people acting outside of the norm, these things don't tend to benefit the Traditions.<br /> <br /> If the event released something big and hard to control (like some kind of entity of malice or of shattered dreams) and that thing rampaged through the city turning it into a no man's land, then I could just about see the Traditions be the main force surviving and protecting people in the rubble. I wouldn't call that being in control of the city, though. And as you said, when the beast was driven back, and the city was repaired and reintegrated into the power and communications networks of America, the Technocracy would be right back there.<br /> <br /> Although...<br /> <br /> I suppose if the main threat was destroyed but the damage was still around- if spirits and cryptids were still running around at the edges of vision- well, the Technocracy would have the dual pressures of rebuilding and proving everything was normal. They would focus on getting their infrastructure up and naturally keep cameras out of the areas most likely to show the abnormal. If the Traditions 'helped' them by keeping the city looking 'stable,' there would be a chance to consolidate power and entrench while the Technocracy was busy.<br /> <br /> Eventually, the local Technocrats might catch on, but then they have a dilemma. They can admit they thoroughly botched the situation and call in reinforcements or they can tell their superiors everything is fine and wait for an opportunity to present itself. Intel on reality deviants suggests they inevitably start fighting each other over meaningless differences (completely unlike the Technocracy... completely), so a waiting game or a psychological war might be the way to go.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T04:05:34-08:00","id":1013674,"title":"","content":"Actually i'm curious how come no one is thinking of the people. New York is one of the most modern urban melting pots in the world. It epitomizes the Western Society that Techncoracy built. The disbelief and paradox backlash for this would be stupendous. And even worse, the New Yorkers won't stand for it... they will be invaded by people who want to take away the modern conveniences and force them into religion and mysticism. And all they wanted was a burger, a beer and a Mets game. So yeah, you will essentially have a city falling apart once the rules of technology start breaking apart and millions seeking to overthrow their tyrants who have taken away their american dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:29:35-08:00","id":1014855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009497-the-traditions-in-charge?p=1013674#post1013674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually i'm curious how come no one is thinking of the people. New York is one of the most modern urban melting pots in the world. It epitomizes the Western Society that Techncoracy built. The disbelief and paradox backlash for this would be stupendous. And even worse, the New Yorkers won't stand for it... they will be invaded by people who want to take away the modern conveniences and force them into religion and mysticism. And all they wanted was a burger, a beer and a Mets game. So yeah, you will essentially have a city falling apart once the rules of technology start breaking apart and millions seeking to overthrow their tyrants who have taken away their american dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Do Akashics and Hermetics have to eschew cell phones and lattes and having bank accounts and using the subway? Some might, but that's a lifestyle choice, not necessarily a requirement to be able to do magic. In fact, the &quot;mini-Consensus&quot; of the Sleepers of NYC are very likely to be the reason why Union-friendly reality doesn't degenerate. Effectively, sort of the &quot;Mythic Thread&quot; of &quot;Modern Western Culture NYC-style&quot; might be very, very strong. Meaning that Paradox will work very much the same for Traditions mages throughout the city. In fact, if there are still Union mages trapped inside the bell jar, they would still have their &quot;coincidental advantage&quot; (they just might not be able to leave... or, if they leave, they can't return). <br /> <br /> Sure, there might be places where it gets VERY thin if it's not a place people pay attention to... but that's very cool in it's own way. Some of those urban legends might become manifest in the cracks in between daily life. Maybe some Lenape monster starts hunting in the subways... Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:46:45-08:00","id":1015705,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone. After reading all the posts, I think I will step back the Traditions in charge idea. Maybe the events of 9/11 did destroy a powerful chantry of the Syndicate but not a total breakdown of the Technocracy. In the aftermath, however, a Traditions cabal worked with a Nephandi to summon a fear Incarna (any ideas of one?) and use some of its power to attack and defeat MECHA. So Traditions not in charge but still a pitched war in New York with increased use of Reality Zones. The Traditions have a dangerous conspiracy with a powerful cabal in league with Nephandi and the Technocracy trying to restart one of two powerful lost chantries. Maybe the Matriarch entity was rescued in some form (trapped on magical floppy disk? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2788-armos-black","name":"Armos Black","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}